  "initial_reflection": {
    "summary": "The run reached Lagavulin with a functional but low-tempo Act 1 deck and lost while the player was already at very low HP. The clearest immediate issue was continuing to choose damage actions during attack turns when survival was no longer secure. Earlier, the run also accumulated optional HP risk and several situational cards without establishing enough damage scaling to end the elite quickly.",
    "lessons": [
      {
        "category": "COMBAT",
        "title": "At critical HP, satisfy survival before adding damage",
        "situation": "When below roughly one or two incoming attacks of lethal range and the enemy is attacking, reassess whether the current damage line actually wins immediately.",
        "lesson": "Do not automatically spend the last energy on another attack. At the Turn 9 state, Defend was legal while HP was 12 and Lagavulin intended to attack; unless the attack sequence is provably lethal, choose the block line over a marginal Strike.",
        "evidence_points": [
          "Turn 9 began at HP 12/74 with Lagavulin at 28 HP and Intent ATTACK; Bash+ was chosen and reduced Lagavulin to 16 HP.",
          "After Bash+, the legal alternatives still included two Strikes, Body Slam, and Defend, and a Strike was chosen, leaving Lagavulin at 9 HP rather than ending the fight.",
          "The run ended in the Lagavulin combat, with the final detailed state showing only 12 HP at the start of this decision sequence."
        ],
        "reasoning": "The selected Strike did not immediately finish the enemy, while Defend was explicitly legal. Because the exact attack damage is unavailable, this is a medium-confidence survival recommendation rather than a claim that Defend definitely prevented death.",
        "confidence": "medium"
      },
      {
        "category": "CARD_REWARD",
        "title": "Prioritize Act 1 damage tempo over additional situational defense",
